  "title": "Benchmark constant-column noise",
  "description": "This experiment restores the benchmark's seeded Gaussian-noise treatment for risk characteristics whose sample standard deviation rounds to zero at six decimals. It replaces those constant cross-sectional values with standard-normal draws before standardization, using seed 1 and a fixed chronological, feature and stock-ID order. Daily factors, residuals and risk estimates are rebuilt consistently. Forecast predictors and nonconstant characteristics remain original. The baseline's zero-exposure treatment remains a separate control.",
